# Awesome GPT Image Prompts

> {{PROMPT_COUNT}} production prompts for OpenAI's GPT Image models, including GPT Image 2.5,
> reproduced verbatim from the {{AUTHOR_COUNT}} people who published them. Each row carries the
> handle that wrote it and a link to the post it came from. Grouped into {{CATEGORY_COUNT}} use
> cases; {{JSON_COUNT}} of them are written as JSON rather than prose. Corpus dated
> {{CORPUS_DATE}}. Maintained by YouArt.

The prompt bodies are third-party text. They are reproduced unchanged, in English only, and
this repository hosts no images. Every readable file listed here is emitted by
`scripts/build.mjs` from `data/prompts.json`, so the counts in it always match the corpus.

The conventional address for an assistant index is <https://youart.ai/llms.txt>, and that is
the primary index for this library. The file you are reading mirrors that section, for agents
that reach the repository first.

The prompt bodies are their authors' work, not ours, and we grant no rights in them; see
LICENSE and ATTRIBUTION.md. The build scripts are MIT. If you quote a prompt, carry its
`author` and its `sourceUrl` with it.

## Machine-readable corpus

- [prompts.json]({{RAW_BASE}}/data/prompts.json): all {{PROMPT_COUNT}} records with their full prompt text, {{PROMPTS_JSON_BYTES}} bytes. Per-row keys: slug, title, category, author, authorUrl, sourceUrl, statusId, isJson, upstream, upstreamStatedTerms, promptSha256, url, prompt. Corpus sha256: {{CORPUS_SHA256}}.
- [prompts.schema.json]({{RAW_BASE}}/data/prompts.schema.json): JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) for the file above. Its root description lists the constraints the build enforces that the schema cannot express.
- [removed.json]({{RAW_BASE}}/data/removed.json): rows withdrawn on request, keyed by the id of the post they came from. It carries no prompt text and no requester identity.
- [README.md]({{RAW_BASE}}/README.md): the human-readable index of all {{PROMPT_COUNT}} prompts, with the writing guide and the FAQ.
- [Run the library on YouArt]({{LIBRARY_URL_TAGGED}}): the same {{PROMPT_COUNT}} prompts on the web, with a composer.

